@startuml seq_005_conflict_resolution
' ============================================================
' Title:     SEQ-005 Conflict Resolution
' Source:    docs/spec/contracts/conflict/
' C4:        ResolveConflict (domain · not peer); artifacts_repository
' Contract:  1.2.0
' ============================================================
!include common/seq_styles.puml

title SEQ-005 Conflict Resolution\nDomain service ResolveConflict (not a C4 peer)\nInvoked by compilation_application / inspections_application

actor "Regulatory Official" as user
participant "clients\n(CLI/Web/Desktop/Mobile)" as SI #EBCB8B
participant "api\n(FastAPI/Pydantic)" as AS #88C0D0
participant "compilation_application\nor inspections_application" as APP #A3BE8C
participant "ResolveConflict\n(domain service · not C4 peer)" as CR #B48EAD
participant "artifacts_repository\n(Object Store)" as SA #81A1C1
participant "finding_events_repository\n(Append-Only)" as FAA #D08770
database "artifacts_store" as ART #4C566A
database "finding_events_store\n(Append-Only Log)" as ES #4C566A

autonumber

== Conflict Detection (in-process during compile / inspect) ==

activate APP
APP -> CR: resolve overlapping rules on frozen CG-IR / directives
activate CR
CR -> CR: scan for within-lineage / cross-lineage conflicts
note right of CR
    Two conflict classes:
    - Within-lineage: deterministic pairs
    - Cross-lineage: advisory warnings
    ResolveConflict is a domain service,
    not a freestanding C4 component.
end note

group Precedence Resolution
    CR -> CR: apply resolution precedence
    note right of CR
        Priority order:
        1. explicit override
        2. directive priority
        3. specificity (narrow wins)
        4. recency (newer wins)
    end note
end

alt Deterministically Resolvable
    CR -> CR: apply deterministic resolution
    CR -> FAA: append ConflictResolved event
    activate FAA
    FAA -> ES: write record
    ES --> FAA: acknowledged
    FAA --> CR: committed
    deactivate FAA
    CR --> APP: resolved
    deactivate CR

else Escalated (Human Review Required)
    CR -> SA: SaveConflictArtifact
    activate SA
    SA -> ART: write-once put (kind=conflict)
    ART --> SA: ok
    SA --> CR: artifact_id
    deactivate SA
    CR --> APP: artifact_id (needs human)
    deactivate CR
    deactivate APP

    == Human Review (artifact-backed) ==

    user -> SI: review conflict artifact
    activate SI
    SI -> AS: GET /artifacts/{artifact_id}
    activate AS
    AS -> SA: GetConflictArtifact
    SA --> AS: ConflictView
    AS --> SI: ConflictView
    deactivate AS

    SI -> AS: POST /artifacts/{artifact_id}/resolutions\n[capability conflict.resolve]
    activate AS
    AS -> SA: record decision on conflict artifact
    activate SA
    SA --> AS: updated
    deactivate SA
    AS -> FAA: append ResolutionDecided event
    activate FAA
    FAA -> ES: write record
    ES --> FAA: acknowledged
    FAA --> AS: committed
    deactivate FAA
    AS --> SI: resolved
    deactivate AS
    SI --> user: confirmation
    deactivate SI
end

note right of CR
    Deterministic resolutions are reproducible
    from directive / CG-IR state (gate AA-05).
    Human resolutions are auditable events +
    artifact updates — not a conflict engine peer.
end note

footer SEQ-005 | Selma Project | Conflict Resolution

@enduml
